DESIGN DECISIONS
-----------------
1. Training pipeline
   - Uses get_cleaned_data_for_ml() from storage/duckdb_queries.py (MinIO → DuckDB → DataFrame)
   - Falls back to _generate_synthetic_data(500) if MinIO bucket empty (allows demo without Flink)
   - ColumnTransformer: OneHotEncoder for categorical fields, passthrough for taxable_income
   - class_weight='balanced' in RandomForest to handle fraud/non-fraud imbalance
   - Logs: parameters, accuracy, precision, recall, F1, confusion matrix PNG, classification report TXT

2. MLflow Model Registry
   - Model registered as 'fraud-detector' on every training run
   - Automatically transitions latest version to 'Staging' after training
   - promote_model.py transitions 'Staging' -> 'Production', archives previous Production

3. OpenLineage emit
   - Emitted as START + COMPLETE events wrapping the training run
   - Input: minio dataset (cleaned-tax/)
   - Output: generic _dataset(namespace='mlflow', name='fraud-detector')
   - Non-fatal: wrapped in try/except so training succeeds even if Marquez is down

4. Synthetic demo data
   - _generate_synthetic_data() produces 500 rows of realistic SA tax records
   - Uses log-normal income distribution (mean=11.5, sigma=1.0)
   - Fraud label: income > 800k AND random < 0.4, OR random < 0.05 (natural imbalance ~10%)

TRAINING OUTPUT (EXPECTED)
--------------------------
  Accuracy : ~0.91
  Precision: ~0.75
  Recall   : ~0.68
  F1 Score : ~0.71
  (higher with more real data from MinIO)

MLFLOW UI
---------
  http://localhost:5001 (after 'make up')
  Experiment: tax-fraud-detection
  Model: fraud-detector (Staging -> Production via make promote)

USAGE
------
  make train           # train with MinIO data (falls back to synthetic if empty)
  make promote         # promote latest Staging to Production
  make promote         # or: python mlflow/promote_model.py --version 2

  # Single run:
  python mlflow/train_fraud_model.py --n-rows 5000 --run-name "rf_v2"
